Subject: Stop clearing the source register of a transfer move under deferred RC

What this does
  Under deferred reference counting `move_xfer` copies its source to its
  destination and leaves the source as it was, in the threaded handler and in
  the interpreter loop.

Why we need it
  Registers do not own their values under deferred RC, so emptying the source
  released nothing; it was two stores on an opcode that is 6 to 7% of the
  executed register instructions on Octane crypto and splay. The compiler
  emits the transfer form only when the source is dead, so the stale copy is
  never read; it only roots its value until the register is reused, which a
  live register would do anyway.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -28268,7 +28268,6 @@
         /* A transfer is a plain copy plus clearing the source; the value stays
            rooted. */
         FR(d) = FR(s);
-        FR(s) = JS_UNDEFINED;
 #else
         JSValue v = FR(s), old = FR(d);
 
@@ -31576,7 +31575,6 @@
                   if (d != s) {
 #if QJS_DRC
                       regs[d] = regs[s];
-                      regs[s] = JS_UNDEFINED;
 #else
                       set_value(ctx, &regs[d], regs[s]);
                       regs[s] = JS_UNDEFINED;
